# admin/.rules

> Canonical rules for `admin/`. `DESIGN.md` is the source of truth for visual style and interaction details; keep this file focused on engineering and product constraints.

`AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are compatibility entrypoints for agent tooling. They must point back to this file instead of duplicating rules. Edit this file first when changing admin engineering rules.

## Design Document

`DESIGN.md` exists and must be read before changing any visible UI, layout, copy, motion, Tailwind token, shadcn-style component composition, responsive behavior, empty state, dialog, table, form, or status presentation.

Use `DESIGN.md` to decide how the admin should look and behave. Use this `.rules` file to decide where code belongs, which APIs and libraries are allowed, and how to validate changes.

If a requested UI change conflicts with `DESIGN.md`, either preserve the design document and choose the closest compliant implementation, or update `DESIGN.md` in the same change when the new pattern should become durable.

## Product Scope

`admin/` is the Rabbit SaaS platform management console. It serves platform staff, not merchant business users.

First-version scope stays narrow:

- Platform admin login and logout.
- Merchant list, create, edit, and enable / disable.
- Merchant user binding and unbinding by existing business user ID.
- Read-only merchant overview for rabbit houses, cages, rabbits, and recent audit records.

Do not add billing, package plans, merchant self-registration, customer support impersonation, cross-merchant business data editing, or platform operation modules unless the task explicitly requests them.

## Engineering Boundaries

- Do not modify backend API contracts from admin UI work unless the user explicitly asks for backend support.
- Do not modify Flutter or Android clients for admin UI tasks.
- Do not bypass the backend SaaS boundaries: platform admin APIs use `/api/admin/**`; merchant business APIs remain under existing `/api/**` flows.
- Preserve read-only boundaries for business production data. Admin may inspect summaries and previews, but must not edit rabbit houses, cages, rabbits, feed, treatment, breeding, or sales data.
- Merchant enable / disable is the only high-risk write operation in the first version.

## Tech Stack

- Package manager: `pnpm`.
- Runtime / build: React + TypeScript + Vite.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS and shadcn-style source components.
- UI primitives: Radix UI where already present.
- Icons: `lucide-react`.
- Request layer: `alova`.
- Toasts: `sonner`.
- Lint: `oxlint`.

Keep Vite on the current newer main major already configured in `package.json`; do not downgrade to avoid transient dependency issues unless a concrete build failure proves it is necessary.

## Directory Responsibilities

- `src/App.tsx`: route tree, authenticated shell wiring, and session-level navigation.
- `src/pages/`: route-level pages only. Pages compose API calls and components, but should not contain reusable UI primitives.
- `src/components/`: domain and layout components shared by admin pages.
- `src/components/ui/`: shadcn-style primitive components. Keep them generic and prop-driven.
- `src/api/`: business API methods. Components must import request functions from here instead of calling raw HTTP clients.
- `src/lib/request.ts`: single alova instance, base URL, token injection, `ApiResponse<T>` unwrapping, and common error handling.
- `src/lib/auth.ts`: platform admin session storage and token access.
- `src/types/`: API and domain TypeScript types.
- `src/index.css`: Tailwind import, semantic color tokens, motion tokens, and global reusable animation classes.
- `DESIGN.md`: canonical visual and interaction design rules.

## API Rules

- Admin login uses `POST /api/admin/auth/login`; do not reuse merchant business login.
- Admin requests must send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` through the alova wrapper.
- Admin requests must not send or require `X-House-Id`.
- API response wrappers with `code !== 0` are business failures and must surface a clear toast or page state.
- `401` clears the admin session and should lead the user back to login through existing route guards.
- Components must not use bare `fetch`, ad hoc `axios`, or inline base URLs.
- Vite development should proxy `/api` to the local backend container, currently `http://127.0.0.1:8080`, unless `VITE_API_BASE_URL` is intentionally provided for another environment.

## UI And Design Rules

Follow `DESIGN.md` before adding any new screen or UI pattern.

Baseline direction:

- Operational SaaS console, not a marketing page.
- Calm, dense, readable, and trustworthy.
- Fixed desktop sidebar, compact mobile header, content constrained to `max-w-7xl`.
- Cards are for contained tools, repeated metrics, tables, dialogs, and empty states only.
- No page sections styled as floating cards inside cards.
- No decorative gradients, blobs, bokeh, oversized hero sections, or illustration-first layouts.

Use semantic Tailwind tokens:

- Prefer `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-secondary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border`, `bg-primary`, `text-destructive`.
- Do not scatter raw status colors in page code.
- Amber is for warnings; red is for errors and destructive actions.
- Main card radius should stay at 8px or less.
- Letter spacing stays `0` or `tracking-normal`.

## Component Rules

- Prefer existing `src/components/ui` primitives before creating custom markup.
- Forms use `FieldGroup`, `Field`, `FieldLabel`, `Input`, `Textarea`, and `Select` patterns.
- Dialogs must include `DialogHeader`, `DialogTitle`, and meaningful `DialogDescription`.
- In the fixed-sidebar shell, desktop dialog content must be centered in the main content pane via the dialog layout viewport and `--admin-sidebar-width`. Do not center dialogs with both `left/top` and `translate(-50%, -50%)`.
- Long dialog forms keep header and footer visible while only the field body scrolls.
- Data display uses `Table`, `Card`, `Badge`, `MetricCard`, `Skeleton`, and `Empty`.
- Buttons use `variant`, `size`, and `asChild` instead of one-off class-heavy button markup.
- Use lucide icons in buttons with `data-icon`; do not manually size button icons unless the shared icon rule changes.
- Loading states should use existing `Skeleton` or `Spinner`.
- Empty states should explain what makes data appear and only show actions available in the current view.

## Motion Rules

- Motion must clarify hierarchy and state changes, not decorate the product.
- Use the global classes from `src/index.css`: `motion-page`, `motion-section`, `motion-list`, `motion-card`, `motion-press`, `motion-dialog-overlay`, and `motion-dialog-content`.
- New animations must preserve `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Avoid looping, bouncing, parallax, large translation, or long staged sequences.
- Cards may lift by 1px on hover; layout-critical surfaces must not move more than 2px.
- Do not create page-local keyframes unless the workflow has a specific need and the rule is added back to `DESIGN.md`.

## Interaction Rules

- Search fields should not query on every keystroke unless debounce, loading feedback, and cancellation behavior are deliberately implemented.
- Filter forms with inline actions must align buttons with the input/select row. Helper or description text belongs in a separate row below the controls when it would push buttons out of alignment.
- Pagination, filters, tabs, and table actions must remain reachable on narrow screens.
- Destructive or high-risk actions use destructive styling and clear verbs, for example `停用商户`, `解绑`, or `删除`.
- Merchant status changes should show a clear success toast naming the completed action.
- Long merchant names, contact fields, OpenID, and IDs must truncate or wrap predictably without overlapping controls.
- Do not add in-app text explaining the UI design, animations, implementation details, or keyboard shortcuts.

## State And React Rules

- Keep route-level data loading inside pages or page-specific hooks.
- Use `useCallback` for async loaders referenced by `useEffect`.
- Keep derived values in `useMemo` only when it improves clarity or prevents repeated non-trivial work.
- Avoid duplicating server state into multiple local states unless the UI explicitly needs staged edits.
- Form dialogs should reset local form state when opening for create / edit.
- Async write actions must guard against duplicate submission through `disabled` or equivalent saving state.

## Dependency And Package Rules

- Use `pnpm --dir admin ...` from the repository root, or run `pnpm ...` inside `admin/`.
- Keep package policy settings in `admin/pnpm-workspace.yaml`, not in the deprecated `pnpm` field in `package.json`.
- Do not relax pnpm supply-chain policies just to pass a transient install. Prefer pinned safe versions or fresh resolution when needed.
- Do not introduce another UI library, CSS framework, request library, or state manager unless the task explicitly requires it.
- Avoid adding dependencies for behavior that is already covered by React, Radix, shadcn-style components, alova, lucide, or existing utilities.

## Validation

Default checks after admin code changes:

```bash
pnpm --dir admin lint
pnpm --dir admin build
```

When changing request behavior or auth:

```bash
pnpm --dir admin dev --host 127.0.0.1
curl -s -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"userName":"admin","password":"admin123456"}' \
  http://127.0.0.1:5173/api/admin/auth/login
```

When changing layout, animation, dialogs, tables, or responsive behavior, verify in a browser at desktop and narrow mobile widths. Check for:

- Console errors.
- Horizontal overflow.
- Text overlap.
- Dialog positioning.
- Table action reachability.
- Reduced-motion behavior where relevant.

Existing acceptable lint warnings may include shadcn Fast Refresh warnings for primitive files that export both component and variant helpers. Do not ignore new warnings without checking the cause.

## Copy Rules

- Use concise operational Chinese.
- Prefer precise verbs over promotional copy.
- Labels should name the business object, not backend table names.
- Error messages and empty states should point to the next practical step.

## Change Discipline

- Keep changes scoped to `admin/` for admin UI tasks.
- Do not reformat unrelated files.
- Do not commit generated `dist/`, `node_modules/`, or local cache changes unless the user explicitly asks.
- If the worktree contains unrelated dirty files, leave them untouched.
